So having proof and having more proof lets you move faster because you don't have to manually check these proofs.

108
00:08:38,573 --> 00:08:41,008
这其实就是智能体验证。
And this is really around agentic validation.

109
00:08:41,198 --> 00:08:44,048
我在我的智能工程视频里讲过这个。
And I talk about that in my agentic engineering video.

110
00:08:44,142 --> 00:08:55,328
但智能体验证是减少代码阅读量的一个核心概念，因为如果 PR
中提前提供了大量的这些证明，你就没必要读那么多代码了。
But agentic validation is a core concept of being able to read less code because if you
have a lot of these proof upfront on the PR, then you don't have to read as much code.

111
00:08:55,488 --> 00:09:00,128
接下来是一个重要的概念，这有点涉及到树状结构的概念，就是叶子节点代码。
Now, the next big concept, and this is kind of in the tree concept, is leaf code.

112
00:09:00,288 --> 00:09:06,848
叶子节点代码是指在隔离状态下编写的代码，或者它在功能门控中被完全隔离开。
A leaf code is really code that is written in isolation or it's completely gated off in a feature gate.

113
00:09:06,928 --> 00:09:14,768
这可能意味着一些独立的组件，你可以通过组件测试或快照测试来验证，对吧？
So this can mean like one off components that you can just validate with like a component test or a snapshot test, right?

114
00:09:14,928 --> 00:09:24,580
或者也许是新的基础设施、新的逻辑，或者是你正在集成的某个新端点，
你可以通过单元测试或集成测试来验证。
Or maybe it's new infrastructure, new logic, maybe a new endpoint that you're integrating with,
and you could just validate that with you know unit tests or integration tests.

115
00:09:24,688 --> 00:09:29,328
只要它们没有整合到主要的生产代码库中，你就可以快速推进。
And as long as they're not integrated to the main production code base, you can move really quickly.

116
00:09:29,550 --> 00:09:32,608
稍后我会讲到你应该怎么做。
And then I'll cover later what you should be doing.

117
00:09:32,846 --> 00:09:37,008
所以对我来说，在审查叶子节点代码时，我花的时间要少得多。
So for me, when I'm reviewing leaf like code, I spend a lot less time.

118
00:09:37,088 --> 00:09:44,608
我几乎只是快速浏览代码，确保没有明显错误或明显不对的地方。
I'm almost just mainly skimming the code and making sure things are not like very off or like something is just obviously wrong.

119
00:09:44,768 --> 00:09:49,808
例如，什么是主干，比如在 reducer 中，reducer 包含很多共享状态。
And for example, what can be a trunk is like you know, in the reducer reducer has a lot of shared state.

120
00:09:49,888 --> 00:09:54,372
假设你在这里更改了一些行为，比如游戏动作中的高级卡片。
So let's say you change some behavior here in this like game action advanced cards.

121
00:09:54,528 --> 00:09:59,248
也许是增加了一种新卡片类型之类的，而你正在修改现有的逻辑。
Maybe there's like a new card type or something like that, and you're changing existing behavior.

122
00:09:59,342 --> 00:10:05,088
如果这个行为没有经过功能门控，那我会花更多时间去审查它，因为这会影响到生产环境，对吧？
And if that behavior is not gated out, then I would spend a lot more time reviewing it because that changes production, right?

123
00:10:05,168 --> 00:10:10,928
而且这会有连锁反应和副作用，所有这些因素都可能非常重要，并影响生产代码，对吧？
And then this has trickle-down effects and side effects, and all these things can really matter and affect production code, right?

124
00:10:11,054 --> 00:10:12,548
所以你真正是基于安全性来把关的。
So you're really anchoring on safety.

125
00:10:12,846 --> 00:10:21,764
所以我们涵盖了如何将代码视为一种梯度，以及你应该如何根据变化来调整你的审查力度，对吧？
So we kind of covered like thinking about code as like this gradient and how you should anchor on changing your effort level, right?

126
00:10:22,128 --> 00:10:25,808
而且在我看来，所有事情都应该以安全为核心。
And in my opinion, everything should be anchored on safety.

127
00:10:25,968 --> 00:10:28,740
哪些是绝对不能改变的控制体验？
What is the control experience that should not change?

128
00:10:28,974 --> 00:10:32,448
如果这次更改出错了，后果会有多严重？
And if this change went wrong, how bad can it be?

129
00:10:32,654 --> 00:10:35,168
然后我能不能撤回这次更改？
And then can I roll this change back?

130
00:10:35,310 --> 00:10:37,764
这其实完全取决于功能门控，对吧？
And then that really just depends on feature gating, right?

131
00:10:38,126 --> 00:10:45,568
所以如果你能回答这些问题，尤其是最后一个，你就可以大幅减少审查每一段代码的时间。
So if you can answer these questions, especially the last one, then you can spend a lot less time reviewing each individual code.

132
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:56,208
现在，还有一件事，在我看来现在并不那么重要，但通常是审查的一部分，
就是 lints 和一些细微的写法差异。
Now, one other thing that is like not that important in my opinion these days, that is
part of like usually reviews is like knits and like little like different ways of writing.

133
00:10:56,368 --> 00:11:00,484
我可以用静态检查来处理大部分这类工作。
And I would just leverage like static checking here to be able to do a lot of that work.

134
00:11:00,782 --> 00:11:04,516
比如类型检查、代码规范检查，还有类似的事情。
So, like type checking, linting, and all those kind of things.

135
00:11:04,878 --> 00:11:07,168
而智能体非常擅长做这些事情。
And agents are really good at doing stuff like this.

136
00:11:07,310 --> 00:11:17,328
所以我们这里有一个 Claude 审查者，它发现了一些代码规范问
题，就像在说我们应该修复它，还有一些风格上的变动，对吧？
So we have a codex reviewer here, and it's like seeing some linting issues, so it's like saying we should fix it as an example,
and here's some like stylistic changes, right?

137
00:11:17,568 --> 00:11:25,808
关于代码审查的一件大事是，我认为过去那种纠结于 lints，
或者觉得“代码应该长成这样”的时代已经过去了。
So, one big thing about code review is that I think the old days of
like having your knits and then like, oh, the code should look this way.

138
00:11:25,968 --> 00:11:28,196
“这是我最喜欢的写法。”
This is my favorite way of writing code.

139
00:11:28,368 --> 00:11:29,568
我觉得这种做法已经过时了。
I think that's kind of dead.

140
00:11:29,728 --> 00:11:41,316
我认为我们写的代码太多了，而且代码变得更加灵活，重构发生的频率也更高，
而且变得更容易操作，尤其是当你想要重构的代码有良好的验证机制时。
I think we write so much code, and code is being a lot more fluid, and refactors are happening a lot more often,
and it's a lot easier to do, especially once like there's good validations for the code that you want to refactor.

141
00:11:41,728 --> 00:11:46,608
我认为这些 lints 不再属于代码审查的讨论范畴了。
I think these kind of knits don't really belong in the conversation of code reviews anymore.

142
00:11:46,768 --> 00:11:50,928
所以，回到最初的问题：我要读代码吗？
So, going back to the original question is do I read the code?

143
00:11:51,150 --> 00:11:53,728
简单的回答是：是的，我仍然阅读很多代码。
The simple answer is yes, I still read a lot of code.

144
00:11:53,934 --> 00:11:56,740
我觉得我读的代码比以前更多了。
I think I read more code than I did before.

145
00:11:57,248 --> 00:12:04,768
但我确实有一个调节旋钮，我会先问自己，这是一个核心变动吗，比如主干上的变动？
But I definitely have this like knob where I I first ask myself, is this a core change, like a trunk change?

146
00:12:04,928 --> 00:12:06,608
它涉及基础设施吗？
And is it touch, It's like an infra?

147
00:12:06,848 --> 00:12:08,688
它有很多依赖项吗？
Does it have a lot of like dependencies?

148
00:12:08,848 --> 00:12:10,208
如果是这样，我就增加审查力度。
If so, I increase it.

149
00:12:10,368 --> 00:12:11,808
然后我问，这安全吗？
And then I say, is this safe?

150
00:12:11,968 --> 00:12:12,768
有门控吗？
Is there gating?

151
00:12:13,198 --> 00:12:14,768
如果出了问题，会发生什么？
If something went wrong, like what can happen?

152
00:12:14,848 --> 00:12:18,244
所以所有这些因素都会影响我审查代码的程度，对吧？
So all of these things really change how much I review the code, right?

153
00:12:18,542 --> 00:12:21,488
而且风险越高，我就投入的精力就越多。
And then the more dangerous it is, the more I spend time.

154
00:12:21,728 --> 00:12:25,328
如果涉及更多这种「单向门」的情况，我就会花更多时间去审查，对吧？
More of that changes a one-way door, I spend more time reviewing, right?

155
00:12:25,488 --> 00:12:31,556
现在，让我们进入点有意思的部分，看看如何利用智能体来辅助你审查代码。
Now, let's get kind of to the fun parts of like looking at how you can use agents to kind of help you review your code.

156
00:12:31,694 --> 00:12:35,968
在我看来，AI 现在其实非常擅长审查代码。
Now, in my opinion, AI is really good at reviewing code already.

157
00:12:36,174 --> 00:12:38,628
我真的认为它比大多数人类都要强。
I actually do think it's better than most humans.

158
00:12:39,118 --> 00:12:41,968
问题是很多人用错了方法。
The issue is a lot of people are doing it wrong.

159
00:12:42,128 --> 00:12:45,968
在我看来，有几件事是你一定要坚持做的。
And in my opinion, there's a few things that you should really anchor on doing.

160
00:12:46,128 --> 00:12:48,208
第一，你应该具备非常出色的审查技能。
One, you should have a really good review skill.

161
00:12:48,368 --> 00:12:52,420
我认为 Claude 和 Codex 都拥有非常出色的内置审查功能。
I think both clock code and codex have really good built reviews.

162
00:12:52,974 --> 00:12:55,172
然后这里就是这个审查智能体。
And then here is the review agent right here.

163
00:12:55,534 --> 00:12:59,684
至于 Claude，则是用 /code review 命令。
And then for clock code, it's slash code review.

164
00:13:00,622 --> 00:13:03,936
所以在我看来，这些都是非常出色的审查智能体。
So these are all both really good review agents, in my opinion.

165
00:13:04,174 --> 00:13:15,908
但有一件很重要的事情是：要使用一个新的子智能体或不同的智能体，
即一个不具备生成代码时所用上下文的智能体，因为智能体会「作弊」。
But one thing that's kind of important to do is to use a new subagent or a different agent,
an agent that doesn't have the context of the code that it was used to create the code because the agents will cheat.

166
00:13:16,238 --> 00:13:18,788
你知道的，你给它提供的所有上下文，它都会利用这些信息来偷懒。
You know, all the context that you gave it, it will cheat.

167
00:13:19,456 --> 00:13:23,204
而且它会非常倾向于依赖之前的对话内容。
and then and it will really try to anchor on like a lot of the previous conversation.

168
00:13:23,376 --> 00:13:32,096
所以你真的需要用一个不同的子智能体，或者是一个被
称为「对抗性审查智能体」的独立智能体来审查代码。
So you really want to review the code with like a different sub agent
or like a separate agent that is called an adversarial review agent.

169
00:13:32,256 --> 00:13:37,776
当你让智能体写 diff 或相关内容时，最好给它一个好的模板可以调用。
And when you have an agent write a diff or thing, just have like a good template that the agent can pull from.

170
00:13:37,998 --> 00:13:42,564
这样你的 PR 看起来就一致，感觉也一致，而且包含关键信息。
So your PRs look the same, they feel the same, they have the important bits.

171
00:13:42,926 --> 00:13:49,936
如果你不给智能体明确的指导，它就会给你写一大段话，就像在讲故事一样。
If you don't give any guidance on the what the agent should really have, it will write you like a giant paragraph, like a story.

172
00:13:50,126 --> 00:14:00,484
说实话，我现在最反感的一点就是，有人提交 PR 或 diff 时，
摘要和测试计划比代码变更本身还要长。
And honestly, that's my biggest pet peeve right now is when people submit PRs or diffs
to review where the summary and test plan is longer than the code changes itself.

173
00:14:00,718 --> 00:14:01,536
所以别成为那种人。
So don't be that guy.

174
00:14:01,696 --> 00:14:09,284
刚才我稍微展示了一下，但我一直在讨论的这些智能体功能都是在运行时、
在生成代码的过程中使用的，也就是你正在运行的部分。
Now I showed this off a little bit, but all the agent stuff that I've been talking about was during runtime,
during the generation of the code, and that's what you're running.

175
00:14:09,614 --> 00:14:21,696
但 Codex 实际上提供了一个这样的集成，你可以把 Codex 审查者添加到 GitHub 上，
它可以在新的 GitHub PR 打开时运行，或者你也可以像这样直接把 Codex 加在这里。
But then Codex actually offers this integration right here where you can add a codex reviewer onto GitHub and it could run on new
GitHub, like you know, PR opens, or you could also like just add codex here like that.

176
00:14:21,776 --> 00:14:24,336
本质上这就是 ChatGPT 的 Codex 连接器。
And essentially it's this chat GPD Codex connector.

177
00:14:24,416 --> 00:14:28,816
而且我认为还有一个稍微不同的模型，是专门针对审查功能进行定制训练的。
And I think there's a separate model slightly that is custom trained just for like reviewing.

178
00:14:28,976 --> 00:14:30,628
当然，所有这些都是要花钱的，对吧？
Now, all of this costs money, right?

179
00:14:31,216 --> 00:14:32,656
不过，这就是一个例子。
But yeah, that's an example.

180
00:14:32,816 --> 00:14:36,976
你还可以做的事情是，比如用 goals 来作为示例。
Another thing you can do is actually use goals as an example.

181
00:14:37,326 --> 00:14:50,532
所以当人们开始使用这些在 GitHub 上审查代码的智能体系统时，会遇到一个常见问题：
在你提交 PR 后，智能体会去执行一些操作，然后给你一堆需要修复的评论。
So one of the common issues that people will run into when they start having these agentic systems that are reviewing their code on
GitHub is that after you submit a PR, the agent will go do stuff and then it'll give you a bunch of comments that you need to fix.

182
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:52,896
有时候会反复沟通很多次。
And sometimes there'll be a lot of back and forth.

183
00:14:52,976 --> 00:14:56,656
你修复了，然后重新提交，接着又是反复沟通。
You fix it and then like you resubmit, and then it'll be like back and forth.

184
00:14:56,846 --> 00:15:00,816
所以你可以做的一件事就是利用目标来全程盯护一个 PR。
So a thing you can do is like just use goals to babysit a PR.

185
00:15:00,910 --> 00:15:03,136
假设我们有一个随机的 PR。
So let's say we had this like random PR.

186
00:15:03,216 --> 00:15:08,656
这是一个草稿，但你可以说：针对这个 PR，你能每小时盯着它一次吗？
This is a draft, but you could just say, for this PR, can you babysit it every hour?

187
00:15:08,846 --> 00:15:15,456
每小时检查一次，确保你处理了来自 Claude 智能体的任何修改请求。
Check it every hour and make sure that you address any changes requests from the codex agent.

188
00:15:15,536 --> 00:15:17,136
它拼写错了，但你明白我的意思。
It misspelled it, but you get the point.

189
00:15:17,262 --> 00:15:27,588
这样做的效果是：它每小时会检查那个 PR，修复任何问题，重
新运行本地验证、智能体验证，更新 PR 说明，然后重新发送。
So, what this will do is every hour it will check that PR and then it will fix any issues, rerun your local validations,
agentic validations, update the PR notes and then resend it.

190
00:15:27,936 --> 00:15:32,816
如果你还没做的话，这些是你应该建立到你自己的技能体系中的内容。
So these are the kind of things that you should build into your own skill if you haven't done so.

191
00:15:33,038 --> 00:15:37,616
没错，在我看来，这些都是一些高层级的、很有用的工具。
But yeah, so those are kind of like the high-level, like useful tools, in my opinion.

192
00:15:37,776 --> 00:15:41,604
在我看来，使用对抗性智能体非常重要。
It's just really important to use adversarial agent, in my opinion.

193
00:15:41,806 --> 00:15:43,216
拥有良好的审查技能。
Have good review skills.

194
00:15:43,342 --> 00:15:46,244
我其实挺喜欢默认的审阅者技能。
I actually just like the default like skill reviewers.

195
00:15:46,576 --> 00:15:56,336
为你的 PR 准备一个模板，如果你愿意可以用我的模板，但一定要有个模板，
让你的 PR 符合该模板，并增加验证证明。
Have a template for your PRs, and you could use my template if you want, but just have a template so it conforms your PRs to that
template and then it adds like validation proof.

196
00:15:56,416 --> 00:15:58,656
你知道的，我们讨论过不同类型的验证。
You know, we talked about the different types of validation.

197
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,924
你真的需要锚定在智能体提供的证明上。
You really want to anchor on the agents giving you proof.

198
00:16:02,318 --> 00:16:04,416
顺便说一下，这实际上会帮助你的 AI 编程。
That will actually help your AI coding, by the way.

199
00:16:04,576 --> 00:16:08,580
然后你提交所有这些内容，并确保锚定在安全和门控上。
And then you just submit all of that, and then you make sure you anchor on safety and gating.

200
00:16:08,878 --> 00:16:11,056
这些就是我考虑的高层级问题。
So these are kind of the high-level things that I think about.

201
00:16:11,216 --> 00:16:22,096
在视频结束前，我还想谈谈如果你这样写代码意味着什么，
也就是你深入阅读一部分代码，而对一些叶子节点只是略读。
Before we end this video, I also want to talk about what it means if you're coding like this,
where you're reading some of the code deeply and you're reading like leaf notes, kind of like skimming it as you're going.

202
00:16:22,256 --> 00:16:29,540
在你编码过程结束时，整个功能的最终产物，就像你会觉得：噢，我做完了。
The end product of that entire feature at the end of your coding session, like you're like, oh, I'm done.

203
00:16:29,806 --> 00:16:34,788
如果你真的这样写代码，实际上你只完成了 80%。
If you actually code in this way, you'll be only actually like 80% done.

204
00:16:35,182 --> 00:16:39,588
所以在这里我想说，即使它可以合并了，我不认为它已经准备好发布了。
So here I'm saying, even if it's merge ready, I don't think it's launch ready.

205
00:16:39,950 --> 00:16:45,764
所以我喜欢做的这步初始步骤，是把所有东西都搞定门控并落地。
So, what I like to do is I call this initial step of like getting everything gated and landed.

206
00:16:45,936 --> 00:16:47,748
我称之为“大轮廓”。
I call that like broad strokes.

207
00:16:47,856 --> 00:16:55,524
我对代码变更进行大轮廓处理，然后最后那 20% 左右的部分才是真正让它达到发布就绪状态。
I'm doing like broad strokes of the code changes, and then this last like 20% or so is really getting something launch ready.

208
00:16:55,758 --> 00:16:59,056
而这正是需要投入大量人工精力的部分。
And this is where a lot of my human like effort comes in.

209
00:16:59,136 --> 00:17:03,684
我在这里会做大量的重构，并对代码库进行清理。
And I do a lot of refactoring here and kind of like cleaning up of the code base.

210
00:17:04,223 --> 00:17:04,464
没错。
Right.

211
00:17:04,704 --> 00:17:07,983
所以在正式发布之前，我实际上会调用一堆智能体。
So I actually have a bunch of agents before I do any launch.

212
00:17:08,144 --> 00:17:10,915
我会审计整段编写的代码。
I like audit the entire code that it was written.

213
00:17:11,214 --> 00:17:13,022
并且从高层维度去思考它。
And I think about it from high level.

